  "term": "dimensionality",
  "definition": "In this context, dimensionality refers to how many variables or features are used to represent complex data. Dimensionality reduction means transforming many measured features into a smaller set of low-dimensional representations so patterns, structure, and relationships can be examined more clearly.",
